  "description": "SMB enumeration drill: Guest SMB → HR share → michael.wrightson password → RID brute → david.orelious → LDAP description → emily.oscars → Backup Operators → reg save → secretsdump. CICADA → FILES SMB password spray → PS transcript → admin creds → psexec.",

  "introduction": "Teaches credential chaining via SMB shares and LDAP—a core OSCP pattern where one foothold unlocks multiple accounts.",
  "mental_model": "Treat SMB as a credential pipeline: enumerate shares, harvest creds, then pivot each new account to discover more (RID brute, LDAP, password spray).",
  "key_principles": [
    "Always try guest/null SMB before brute-forcing",
    "RID brute when you have one valid domain user",
    "Check LDAP description fields for stored creds",
    "Backup Operators can read SAM via reg save",
    "Password spray laterally with every new credential"
  ],

